{"id": "unknown-2026-06-24-008", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Energy sharing, storage reshaping Slovenia’s PV market", "content": "<p><b>pv magazine</b> spoke with Nina Hojnik, General Manager of the Slovenian Photovoltaic Association at the Smarter E tradeshow in Munich, about the launch of energy sharing and its first registrations, alongside a residential rebound driven by solar-plus-storage.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/energy-sharing-storage-reshaping-slovenias-pv-market/\">Energy sharing, storage reshaping Slovenia’s PV market</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/energy-sharing-storage-reshaping-slovenias-pv-market/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-24-009", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Escaping the energy straitjacket", "content": "<p>Europe’s split grid infrastructure and lack of central planning mean it fails to use its renewables. It is stuck in volatile prices driven by reliance on imported fossil fuels. Treating the system as one network rather than separate national grids would unlock PV, storage and wind, says Christian Kjaer, executive director at Supergrid Europe.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/escaping-the-energy-straitjacket/\">Escaping the energy straitjacket</a> appeared first o", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/escaping-the-energy-straitjacket/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-24-010", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "AlphaESS introducing AlphaConnect connectivity platform for energy storage projects", "content": "<p>The manufacturer is expanding into utility-scale storage and integrated energy solutions to meet the evolving needs of the European market, according to Thomas Yuan, Chairman of AlphaESS.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/alphaess-introducing-alphaconnect-connectivity-platform-for-energy-storage-projects/\">AlphaESS introducing AlphaConnect connectivity platform for energy storage projects</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Glo", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/alphaess-introducing-alphaconnect-connectivity-platform-for-energy-storage-projects/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "trina-2026-06-24-011", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["trina"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Trina Solar debuts 670 W TOPCon module for utility scale PV", "content": "<p>The new module can reportedly achieve a power conversion efficiency of up to 24.8% and a bifaciality factor of over 85%. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/trina-solar-debuts-670-w-topcon-module-for-utility-scale-pv/\">Trina Solar debuts 670 W TOPCon module for utility scale PV</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/trina-solar-debuts-670-w-topcon-module-for-utility-scale-pv/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-24-012", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "RCT Group launches unit for space solar applications", "content": "<p>The German company said its new RCT Space targets low-earth orbit customers. It expects commercial deliveries to begin in 2027. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/rct-group-launches-unit-for-space-solar-applications/\">RCT Group launches unit for space solar applications</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/rct-group-launches-unit-for-space-solar-applications/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-24-013", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Feeding Europe’s AI energy demand", "content": "<p>On one hand, European policymakers are aiming for climate neutrality by 2050. On the other, they’re aiming to at least triple the region’s data center market by the mid-2030s to conserve European digital sovereignty and economic competitiveness. Is it possible to do both? Not without demand-side flexibility, cross-border electricity trading, and smarter integration of renewable energy assets. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/feeding-europes-ai-energy-demand/\">F", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/feeding-europes-ai-energy-demand/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-24-014", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["leading"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Solar industry’s shift from silver presents potential barrier for panel recycling", "content": "<p>Efforts among leading manufacturers to produce solar cells using base metals instead of silver in a bid to reduce costs could pose a threat to the future economic viability of recycling end-of-life panels. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/solar-industrys-shift-from-silver-presents-potential-barrier-for-panel-recycling/\">Solar industry’s shift from silver presents potential barrier for panel recycling</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">p", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/solar-industrys-shift-from-silver-presents-potential-barrier-for-panel-recycling/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-24-015", "date": "2026-06-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 26, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["breakthrough"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Catalyst breakthrough could accelerate green hydrogen production", "content": "<p>An international research team, including scientists from the University of Adelaide, have developed a highly efficient microscopic iridium catalyst that could represent an important step toward more affordable and efficient green hydrogen production. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/catalyst-breakthrough-could-accelerate-green-hydrogen-production/\">Catalyst breakthrough could accelerate green hydrogen production</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-ma", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/24/catalyst-breakthrough-could-accelerate-green-hydrogen-production/", "type": "rss"}]}
